# Storyboard — {{TITLE}}

Authoritative slide manifest for this deck. The build tooling consumes the
manifest order; lint cross-checks declared fact IDs against fragment comments
and the registry.

**This file is the spec.** A build only supersedes it by amending it in the
same unit of work: if a fix changes mandated wording or the fact-ID set, the
detail block and the manifest row change in that same commit. A storyboard
that lags the deck is worse than no storyboard.

Rules in force for every slide:
- Every number comes from a registry row. Filed or audited values beat
  presentation values.
- Public footnotes name sources and dates. Registry IDs never render.
- Any row flagged unverified, deck-only, or conflicting is either dropped,
  reframed, or labelled on the slide face. Never shipped quietly.
- Archetype names refer to the shipped library (see the skill's
  `references/archetypes.md`); a deck-local layout uses an `x-` prefix and is
  registered in `ARCHETYPES.md`.

